{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/KIRO7Seattle/posts/understand-the-supreme-courts-5-4-decision-allowing-post-election-day-ballot-cou/1439092138253846/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/KIRO7Seattle/posts/understand-the-supreme-courts-5-4-decision-allowing-post-election-day-ballot-cou/1439092138253846/","title":"KIRO 7 News","description":"Understand the Supreme Court's 5-4 decision allowing post-Election Day ballot counting.","language":"en","text":"Understand the Supreme Court's 5-4 decision allowing post-Election Day ballot counting.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n136 comments\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nJonathan Levy-Wolins\n\nIts really simple. All votes matter. All votes that are cast before or on election day deserve to be counted.\n\n18\n\nView all 12 replies\n\nLou Kitz\n\nThey still need to be postmarked by election day. A silver lining to a dark cloud.\n\n6\n\nView all 16 replies\n\nPaul Lukas\n\nAll of a sudden... the court is legitimate again. lmao\n\n4\n\nView all 8 replies\n\nDanny Ventura\n\nWait, they didn't say that you can't postmark all ballots as the day AFTER an election\n\nBen Garrott\n\nAs long as they are mailed in by 8pm on Election Day, I see no issues.\n\n7\n\nSandra GK Mango\n\nOur military members need to be able to vote, regardless of what Trump thinks!\n\n3\n\nView all 6 replies\n\nTom Nickel\n\nI find it totally acceptable to count the votes that are post marked by the correct day.\n\n2\n\nView 1 reply\n\nRobin Kiehn\n\nGood to see some common sense coming out of SCOTUS.\n\n6\n\nJay Morgan\n\nProve election fraud with tangible evidence and I'll vote for Trump. I want iron clad, real evidence that proves illegals vote in big numbers. Not 1 not 7 but show me enough to switch a vote. Prove the election was stolen\n\n5\n\nView all 2 replies\n\nTraci Kelly\n\nIt should've been 9-0.\n\n8\n\nView 1 reply","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2496.2175249966094,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}